WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The relationships that we have with our siblings are often the longest-lasting relationships of our lives. Brothers and sisters are our first childhood playmates and our first rivals. In adulthood, siblings can be a source of friendship and emotional support. They're the only other people in the world who remember and understand exactly what it was like to grow up within our family. Yet despite their importance, sibling relationships are often overlooked and understudied, are seen as less important than other relationships such as romantic partnerships and parent-child bonds.
我们与兄弟姐妹之间的关系通常是我们一生中最持久的关系。兄弟姐妹是我们童年最早的玩伴，也是我们最早的竞争对手。在成年后，兄弟姐妹可以成为友谊和情感支持的源泉。他们是世界上仅有的、能够准确记得并理解我们在同一个家庭中长大是什么感觉的其他人。然而，尽管兄弟姐妹关系如此重要，它却经常被忽视和缺乏研究，被认为不如浪漫伴侣和亲子纽带等其他关系那么重要。

2
00:00:35.000 --> 00:01:13.000
But psychologists and other researchers have insights to offer on how our siblings influence our lives from childhood through adulthood. So how can we get the most out of these relationships? How do our siblings affect us as children and as adults? What can parents do to help foster close relationships among their children? When parents play favorites, how does that affect the sibling bond? What can people do in adulthood to maintain and improve relationships with their own siblings? And what does the research say about the diverse types of sibling relationships that are more common than ever, such as half-siblings, step-siblings, and others?
但心理学家和其他研究人员为我们提供了深刻见解，让我们了解兄弟姐妹如何从童年到成年影响我们的人生。那么，我们如何才能最大程度地利用这些关系呢？兄弟姐妹在童年和成年期如何影响我们？父母可以做些什么来帮助增进孩子之间的亲密关系？当父母偏心时，会对兄弟姐妹的纽带产生什么影响？成年人可以做些什么来维持和改善与自己兄弟姐妹的关系？关于现在比以往任何时候都更常见的各种类型的兄弟姐妹关系（如同父异母/同母异父的兄弟姐妹、继兄弟姐妹等），研究是怎么说的？

